{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/TASK.md'","aggregated_output":"# Task: H03 — Cross-module public-function rename\n\n> Held-out RFC-0005 suite · Shape: Cross-module refactor (1/2).\n> You are maintaining an **existing correct system**; do not rewrite it from\n> scratch. Change only what the task requires.\n\n## Base (workspace)\n\nThe workspace contains a correct, deterministic pricing program with three\nmodules:\n\n- `pricing.rules` — exports the public price-adjustment function\n  `adjust_price(base, pct)` returning the adjusted price;\n- `checkout.quote` — calls that function to compute a quote;\n- `reports.preview` — calls that function to render a preview line.\n\nThe program is driven by the environment variable `H03_SCENARIO` and prints\ndeterministic lines. There is no persistence, no wall-clock dependency, and no\nstate machine.\n\n## Required change\n\nRename the public function in `pricing.rules` from `adjust_price` to\n`apply_adjustment`:\n\n1. `apply_adjustment` becomes the **official public export** of\n   `pricing.rules`;\n2. every cross-module qualified caller (`checkout.quote`, `reports.preview`)\n   must call the new name;\n3. the old public name `adjust_price` is **no longer a valid public API** of\n   the module;\n4. behavior must remain **exactly identical** (same outputs for the same\n   inputs);\n5. no parameter changes, no return-type changes, no schema/persistence\n   changes, no state-machine changes.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe hidden verifier rebuilds the project, drives the compiled program through\nscenarios, and additionally checks **external integration consumers**:\n\n- a consumer that calls the new `apply_adjustment` API must compile and run;\n- a consumer that still calls the old `adjust_price` API must fail to compile\n  against the new public surface;\n- quote / preview behavior must be unchanged.\n\nThe workspace exposes only the program state and this task; the verifier is\nnot visible to you.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
